cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the methods it builds on (references)."
title: "Theme Worlds: seamless 360-degree panoramas from stock Stable Diffusion v1.5"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Melis
    given-names: Marlen
    affiliation: KAIST
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarlenMM/theme-worlds"
url: "https://marlenmm.github.io/theme-worlds/"
keywords:
  - diffusion models
  - MultiDiffusion
  - panorama generation
  - Stable Diffusion
  - classifier-free guidance
  - composable diffusion
abstract: >-
  A MultiDiffusion sampler written from scratch for stock Stable Diffusion v1.5 that produces seamless
  wrap-around panoramas: circular windows make the loop a property of the sampling rather than a
  post-process, and multi-branch conditioning combines two themes without truncating either prompt at
  CLIP's 77-token limit. Mean seam ratio 1.12 over 28 panoramas; no training and no source images.
  Built for the Visual Content Contest of KAIST AIC.20000 (Fall 2026).
